              "observablePerformanceEn": "100000 Pa×0.00200 m³=200 J. Expansion gives W_on=-200 J and ΔU=+300 J. With equal constant system/external pressure and only pV work, ΔH=ΔU+pΔV=500 J=Q_p. The rigid vessel has ΔV=0, W_on=0 and ΔU=500 J=Q_v. Work transfer, not destroyed energy, explains the difference. The sketch shows 500 J in, 200 J work out and a 300 J U increase. The processes need not have identical final states; the U/H relations depend on the stated conditions."
