              "observablePerformanceEn": "Describe hydrolysis, terminal-group oxidation and beta oxidation for the model, tracking carbon/product class. Assess whether80%disappearance proves mineralisation. Specify a genuine further measurement; Expected:Ester hydrolysis consumes water and cleaves the ester link; C12 alcohol oxidises throughC12 aldehyde toC12 acid without immediate carbon cleavage. After activation, beta-oxidation cycles removeC2 units; an ideal saturatedC12 chain yields six acetyl units after five shortening cycles. This is not itself completeCO2 measurement.80%parent-substance disappearance can include intermediates, sorption/biomass;30%CO2 does not show full mineralisation. Carbon balance, degradates and aquatic effects are needed; pathways depend on substance/conditions."
